From 1b05af627f32a0ecdb952da43796cdedaf64e8a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 11:17:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0125 -- render and scene-construct phase
 brackets, empty black-fill skip

Consolidates 0125, 0126, 0133, 0135, 0136, 0137, 0138, 0162, 0166 and the
counter fields that 0167's clip accounting (0170-0174) reads.

Why. After the present was cut, render_backbuffer (5.04 ms/tick, 20.2% of a
16-bit frame) and scene_construct (24%) were the largest terms nobody had
opened, and this campaign's own record is that naming such a term from
reading was wrong twice. So each is bracketed and counted rather than
guessed at:
- 0125: render_backbuffer structure (batches, per-batch clears and their
  area, sprites, composited pixels) and a bracket on the blitting half.
- 0126: the background restore timed on its own, with pixels copied, whole
  frames and the slow (non-memcpy) arm counted. Upstream's own comment on
  that call says it can take up to half the CPU at high resolutions.
- 0133 and 0135: four sc_* brackets on the scene construction stages and
  five inside construct_room_view (preroom, prep objects, prep characters,
  draw list, viewports).
- 0162: span count and a coarse length histogram for the restore loop.
- 0166: the largest sprite's dimensions, so a tail frame can be attributed to
  one element or to many.
- 0137: whole-frame fills counted.

Two of these change what executes, not only what is measured:
- 0136: update_invalid_region(Bitmap*, color_t, ...) now returns early when
  there are no dirty regions, as its bitmap overload already did. Without it
  a 360-row scan with a 36-byte memcmp per row ran to discover nothing to
  fill (sc_preroom measured 1,737 ms, 60% of construct_room_view).
- 0138: the per-row loop tests numSpans before the identical-row memcmp.
  The comment argues the output is identical (empty rows merge and then fill
  nothing); the DOSBox-X screenshot-hash gate is what checks it.

The DosPortTickTiming hunk is carried whole, so it also declares the rb_clip_*
and rb_gui_* fields whose users arrive in 0167.

Provenance of this export (2026-09-21): these edits sat uncommitted in the
vendor tree from patch 0123 onward, which is why every gate cell since said
build_dirty=1. They were made under one campaign-wide patch counter shared
with vendor/SDL, and each hunk carries its number in an in-source comment.
Intermediate states were never committed, so this patch is a hunk-level
partition of the final tree by concern, attributed by those comments -- not a
replay of the order the edits were made in, and its intermediate state was not
built on its own. The numbers named below are the ones found in its hunks.

